# Both games from power-on: intro, title, menus, character select, match --
# held to one frame each by the barrier the whole way, not just once they are
# fighting. The port boots the way the console does rather than jumping to a
# debug match, and takes the same recorded route as a pad script, so the two
# are pressing the same buttons on the same frames from the title screen on.
#
#   tools/pc_lockstep.py sync_title --size 1200x900
#
# Nothing is skipped and nothing about where each side is is ignored: `mode`
# and `scene` are compared like everything else, every frame, so the run stops
# the moment the two are on different screens. That is the point -- the port's
# stage select is not ported yet (MnSelectStageDataTable is a bare table of
# 4-byte descriptor offsets and a struct of 8-byte pointers cannot be laid over
# it), and this case is supposed to say so rather than route around it.
description: both games from the title screen, in step every frame
# Both sides run freely until they reach the intro (mode 24), wait there for
# each other, and are only then held to one frame each -- so how long each
# takes to boot does not matter. The route's frame numbers are measured from
# the console's arrival there (route_zero), which is what makes the same
# numbers mean the same moment on both.
rendezvous: 24
route_zero: 187
# The port acts on a press ~2 frames after it arrives, the console ~5, so the
# same press on the same frame moves the port's screen first every time.
# Measured at three transitions: 3, 2, 2 frames. The port's script is delayed
# to match. Same offset match_move.case carries as ref_shift: 3.
port_input_lag: 3
# A scene change lands up to a frame apart even after that compensation, so
# mode and scene may disagree for this many frames while one side is
# mid-transition. Bounded on purpose: a port sitting on the wrong screen, or
# never reaching one, disagrees for good and still stops the run.
scene_skew: 4
# The console reaches the match through screens the port skips, so it burns RNG
# draws the port never makes. rng_draws carries the comparable part of that.
ignore: seed
ref_input: 236:+START
ref_input: 240:-START
ref_input: 400:+START
ref_input: 404:-START
